<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>France 24 - International breaking news, top stories and headlines</title><subtitle type="html">Breaking news and world news from France 24 on Business, Sports, Culture. Video news. News from the US, Europe, Asia Pacific, Africa, Middle East, America</subtitle><id>https://www.france24.com/en/rss</id><updated>2026-09-04T12:49:37Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/rss" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Trump raises doubts over support for Britain in Falklands dispute with Argentina</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:fd5d827b0e9ef5730d61693a2275bf9cb348595526d4055fb5e2fe006d60db46</id><updated>2026-09-04T12:48:29Z</updated><published>2026-09-04T12:46:18Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260904-trump-raises-doubts-over-support-for-britain-in-falklands-dispute-with-argentina--4d7bdd70d5f1.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260904-trump-raises-doubts-over-support-for-britain-in-falklands-dispute-with-argentina" /><summary type="html">US President Donald Trump raised doubts about whether the United States would support Britain in another conflict over the Falkland Islands in an interview with a British broadcaster aired Thursday, injecting new tension into the long-standing dispute over the British-controlled archipelago also claimed by Argentina. Trump's comments came as his ideological ally, Argentine President Javier Milei, prepared to deliver a televised national address about what his government has described as diplomatic progress over the islands that lie about 480 kilometers off Argentina’s coast in the South Atlantic. FRANCE 24's International Affairs Editor Rochelle Ferguson-Bouyahe tells us more.</summary></entry><entry><title>France announces €1 billion aid for farmers recovering from drought, heatwaves</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b71b7a9d113b8afd35cfb87bf52b72e8b1ed4d94d9386466e8c342975ffc3b66</id><updated>2026-09-04T12:48:31Z</updated><published>2026-09-04T12:44:54Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/france/20260904-france-announces-_1-billion-aid-for-farmers-recovering-from-drought-heatwaves--eeb3d273204e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/france/20260904-france-announces-%E2%82%AC1-billion-aid-for-farmers-recovering-from-drought-heatwaves" /><summary type="html">France on Friday allocated more than €1 billion in aid to support farmers recovering from droughts after a brutal, record-breaking summer. The allocation includes €520 million for rapid payments to ‌help farmers deal with weather damage and a €235 million recovery ​fund to buy seeds, plants and ​animal feed, Agriculture Minister Annie Genevard said.</summary><category term="France" /></entry><entry><title>UK reasserts Falklands sovereignty amid Milei claim and Trump comments</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ffd3dad99b40e84002364f08233e77f594953b358d88b8b13bb34486be29d7c8</id><updated>2026-09-04T12:48:34Z</updated><published>2026-09-04T12:44:49Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260904-uk-reasserts-falklands-sovereignty-amid-milei-claim-and-trump-comments--3ec0ef408ae5.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260904-uk-reasserts-falklands-sovereignty-amid-milei-claim-and-trump-comments" /><summary type="html">Britain insisted Friday that the Falkland Islands "are British" after Argentine President Javier Milei suggested the "winds of change" now favoured his country's claim to the archipelago, citing Washington's readiness to reconsider its neutrality in the dispute. The islands' fate returned to the headlines after US President Donald Trump threatened to wade into the dispute, while a British-Israeli oil project near the islands stoked anger in Argentina. FRANCE 24's London correspondent, Bénédicte Paviot, gives an inside look at Downing Street's reaction to these developments.</summary></entry><entry><title>Israeli minister unveils plan to remove Gaza's population over seven years</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:68d0a934921d5349f0fd35720eb2f90d27a3a3c847a583ec6c404d2d131c5d8c</id><updated>2026-09-04T12:48:37Z</updated><published>2026-09-04T12:43:50Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260904-israeli-minister-unveils-plan-to-remove-gaza-s-population-over-seven-years--40655bf68719.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260904-israeli-minister-unveils-plan-to-remove-gaza-s-population-over-seven-years" /><summary type="html">Israel's far-right National Security Minister Itamar Ben Gvir set out a plan on Thursday to remove Palestinians from the Gaza Strip and send them abroad. Speaking in the run-up to close-fought Israeli elections, he said the plan aimed to see the departure of 250,000 Palestinians from Gaza in the first year, followed by the rest of the roughly two million residents over the following six years. Forced displacement of civilians in occupied territory is considered a war crime under the Geneva Conventions.</summary></entry><entry><title>'Moroccans are desperate: Years of political crackdown and lack of economic opportunities'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8f8d4c428534dd2a761ccdfcfa944712b43533cf462dfc26b3ac40e10a6becc7</id><updated>2026-09-04T12:48:40Z</updated><published>2026-09-04T12:30:37Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20260904-moroccans-are-desperate-years-of-political-crackdown-and-lack-of-economic-opportunities--0197ef1ebe1f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20260904-moroccans-are-desperate-years-of-political-crackdown-and-lack-of-economic-opportunities" /><summary type="html">François Picard is pleased to welcome Aida Alami, New York Times World contributor. Drawing on her own field reporting at the Moroccan border, Alami challenges attempts to explain the mass crossing primarily through a theory of deliberate state orchestration. While acknowledging both Morocco’s history of leveraging migration in its relations with Spain and the possibility that security forces made tactical decisions on the day, Alami insists on distinguishing evidence from inference. Her reporting instead points toward an interaction between online misinformation, overwhelmed security forces, and a population already primed to migrate by political repression and limited economic opportunity.</summary><category term="Spotlight" /></entry><entry><title>Haute Couture, autumn-winter 2026/27: Make way for the independent labels</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:55565bf49c684781e8f5af6c6d45257f2b2b0cf048dcd3ef570b6c631d9034f8</id><updated>2026-09-04T12:48:43Z</updated><published>2026-09-04T12:04:25Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/fashion/20260904-haute-couture-autumn-winter-2026-27-make-way-for-the-independent-labels--e3afae87e262.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/fashion/20260904-haute-couture-autumn-winter-2026-27-make-way-for-the-independent-labels" /><summary type="html">Some couturiers get to modernise houses owned by luxury groups. Among them is Duran Lantink, who draws on Jean Paul Gaultier's ballet-costume era for his inspiration. Independent houses, by contrast, must create from scratch. Iris van Herpen turns to science. Rahul Mishra finds inspiration in the beauty of Hindu goddesses. Imane Ayissi pays tribute to his late mother. Finally, Kevin Germanier keeps celebrating the most desirable approach to recycling imaginable.</summary><category term="Fashion" /></entry><entry><title>US state of Louisiana in battle over electoral map</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:955fbba501286f6fe12b55783d5fbdd19fbcedd95453f9f3bf0eeb5b797c9e97</id><updated>2026-09-04T12:48:47Z</updated><published>2026-09-04T12:03:26Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/reporters/20260904-us-state-of-louisiana-in-battle-over-electoral-map-midterm-elections--ade161a79150.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/reporters/20260904-us-state-of-louisiana-in-battle-over-electoral-map-midterm-elections" /><summary type="html">With just two months to go before the US midterm elections, the battle for votes is in full swing. Our reporter Fanny Allard has been to the state of Louisiana, where a redistricting row is playing out with far-reaching implications for racial equality.</summary><category term="Reporters" /></entry><entry><title>Mass burial reveals hidden toll of Algeria’s deadly ‘Black Wednesday’ wildfires</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3aafb7b1a4765d677658ac8384ff1f339fda8705b048f31c2c0557d31cc649d5</id><updated>2026-09-04T12:48:50Z</updated><published>2026-09-04T11:33:04Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/africa/20260904-mass-burial-algeria-black-wednesday-deadly-wildfires--e2ca45613885.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/africa/20260904-mass-burial-algeria-black-wednesday-deadly-wildfires" /><summary type="html">Wildfires ripped across northeastern Algeria in late August. Photos and videos showing the mass burial of several dozen people have raised questions about the real death toll of the fires as Algerian authorities haven’t shared new numbers since August 26. A number of Moroccan social media accounts have also been sharing disinformation about the fires.</summary><category term="Africa" /></entry><entry><title>Stability or fiasco? Giorgia Meloni becomes longest-serving Italian PM</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:443d7ab0d28dbc82bb24bba28d882a69dbc2346ac2b2e6dfe8d2aa43182041ef</id><updated>2026-09-04T12:48:53Z</updated><published>2026-09-04T10:29:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/press-review/20260904-stability-or-fiasco-giorgia-meloni-becomes-longest-serving-italian-pm--c8766e845af9.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/press-review/20260904-stability-or-fiasco-giorgia-meloni-becomes-longest-serving-italian-pm" /><summary type="html">PRESS REVIEW – Friday, September 4: Italy's Giorgia Meloni becomes the longest-serving prime minister in Italy's postwar history. While she's celebrated by the rightwing press, the leftwing press say her leadership is a fiasco. Also, is Europe gearing up for a chaotic winter? Concern is mounting after the UN warned of a "supersized" El Niño phenomenon that could bring heavy rains and snow. Plus we look at tributes to Gloria Steinem, journalist and women's rights icon, who has died at 92.</summary><category term="Press Review" /></entry><entry><title>Two trapped workers rescued from mud-clogged tunnel 9 days after Nepal floods</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:75b4c909592346ce32fb00d0102df3edbbc35b39d25d365a7af1cb2915d26dca</id><updated>2026-09-04T12:48:55Z</updated><published>2026-09-04T10:12:49Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260904-two-trapped-workers-rescued-from-mud-clogged-tunnel-9-days-after-nepal-floods--395bdff0000d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260904-two-trapped-workers-rescued-from-mud-clogged-tunnel-9-days-after-nepal-floods" /><summary type="html">Nine days after catastrophic floods hit Nepal, hope emerges from the dark as two workers have been rescued from a collapsed tunnel. They are receiving treatment as emergency crews race to find more survivors. The floods killed more than 1,200 people and left over 5,000 missing. An estimated 115 people are still believed trapped in the tunnel.</summary></entry><entry><title>Argentina's Milei escalates Falklands dispute in sovereignty push against Britain</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:39a42909987ae2da7dcd592b4f808786e3b492f9e736cd326c7dfc6a7f8adff7</id><updated>2026-09-04T12:48:59Z</updated><published>2026-09-04T10:07:32Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260904-argentina-s-milei-escalates-falklands-dispute-in-sovereignty-push-against-britain--a5cb7dd51916.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260904-argentina-s-milei-escalates-falklands-dispute-in-sovereignty-push-against-britain" /><summary type="html">Argentine President Javier Milei said he would sanction oil companies drilling in the Falkland Islands, the British overseas territory claimed by Argentina, in a move which could escalate tensions with London. Milei's comments in a televised national ​address on Thursday came ‌days after US President Donald Trump said he was reviewing the United States' neutral position on the ⁠remote archipelago in the South Atlantic.</summary></entry><entry><title>New fears of oil supply disruption as US-Iran hostilities resume</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:65307c27378ab781b95d21bd7f669f2c1dd334ebab97a7929ef0c255b049c1eb</id><updated>2026-09-04T12:49:01Z</updated><published>2026-09-04T09:56:46Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260904-new-fears-of-oil-supply-disruption-as-us-iran-hostilities-resume--0869871bdd37.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260904-new-fears-of-oil-supply-disruption-as-us-iran-hostilities-resume" /><summary type="html">Renewed hostilities between the United States and Iran have brought back fears of oil supply disruption. Prices are on track for their steepest weekly gain since mid-July, up 7.6%, as the US-Iran war enters its seventh month. Twenty-five percent of the world's oil supply comes through the Strait of Hormuz, which has been blocked since the beginning of the war. FRANCE 24's international affairs editor Philip Turle gives more details.</summary></entry><entry><title>From forced labour to World Heritage: Sao Tome's colonial plantations</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c6b9172d9250369a9a6ce117ed956085b5e0d42e7fb4eeea5bf73fd5fe38a0e3</id><updated>2026-09-04T12:49:04Z</updated><published>2026-09-04T09:43:27Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260904-from-forced-labour-to-world-heritage-sao-tome-s-colonial-plantations--546b308a56be.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260904-from-forced-labour-to-world-heritage-sao-tome-s-colonial-plantations" /><summary type="html">Sao Tome and Principe's "Rocas" – colonial-era plantations – have been added to the UNESCO World Heritage List in July 2026, in recognition of their architecture and their fundamental importance to the country’s history. While the majority of them now lie derelict, they are attracting increasing interest from investors keen to develop the tourism potential of the history-steeped buildings.</summary></entry><entry><title>IOM ramps up emergency aid in Lake Chad as thousands flee Boko Haram</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5c1a6e4334319fd302bc72a745c95ed4f576ab8ace87b55647f489a7c8164a5a</id><updated>2026-09-04T12:49:07Z</updated><published>2026-09-04T09:40:30Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260904-iom-ramps-up-emergency-aid-in-lake-chad-as-thousands-flee-boko-haram--1e7114a81065.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260904-iom-ramps-up-emergency-aid-in-lake-chad-as-thousands-flee-boko-haram" /><summary type="html">More than 75,000 people have been newly displaced within Chad’s Lake Province following a resurgence in Boko Haram attacks in recent months. That is the latest figure from the International Organization for Migration, which is providing emergency assistance to meet their most immediate needs. Most of these tens of thousands of people have fled the islands of Lake Chad, seeking safety in towns and villages further away from the island areas. FRANCE 24's Harold Girard reports.</summary></entry><entry><title>#Nepal: Two flood survivors rescued from hydropower tunnel</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:56a154c5f30918795a23780379054883541cfd88859d2059c2322898cdf349d3</id><updated>2026-09-04T12:49:10Z</updated><published>2026-09-04T09:38:17Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260904-nepal-two-flood-survivors-rescued-from-hydropower-tunnel--4c0fb43a0f62.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260904-nepal-two-flood-survivors-rescued-from-hydropower-tunnel" /><summary type="html">In a video posted to social media on September 4, the Nepali #army announced it had rescued two workers trapped in a hydropower tunnel. The rescue brings hope of reaching over a dozen others thought to be trapped inside the tunnel. Both men were flown to a hospital in #Kathmandu. The floods killed more than 1,200 people, and over 5,000 are still missing.</summary></entry><entry><title>Nepal flood aftermath: Zip lines carry medicine as survivors relive the horror</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:943bdd101eccb9f40dea910c3480f08480777f8443a74d5114f9c1b408fab42b</id><updated>2026-09-04T12:49:13Z</updated><published>2026-09-04T09:37:55Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260904-nepal-flood-aftermath-zip-lines-carry-medicine-as-survivors-relive-the-horror--85648f5b3de5.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260904-nepal-flood-aftermath-zip-lines-carry-medicine-as-survivors-relive-the-horror" /><summary type="html">Eight days after disastrous floods in Nepal, as the death toll continues to rise, survivors are left struggling to access basic necessities. The shortages are adding to the hardships of those living in temporary shelters after having lost homes and belongings. While some are focusing on ensuring food and medicine reach devastated areas, many are now left grappling with the psychological trauma of the disaster.</summary></entry><entry><title>Italy weighs the results as Giorgia Meloni’s government sets a longevity record</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:75e2a7dbbcd5161fe72f1cb33daa9796ee51f545df396c77823f0b1c520530b8</id><updated>2026-09-04T12:49:16Z</updated><published>2026-09-04T09:36:05Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260904-italy-weighs-the-results-as-giorgia-meloni-s-government-sets-a-longevity-record--1526a8a44ffb.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260904-italy-weighs-the-results-as-giorgia-meloni-s-government-sets-a-longevity-record" /><summary type="html">In a country where governments are famously short-lived, the perceived success of Italian Premier Giorgia Meloni has often been attributed to her survival skills rather than her accomplishments.   The record is likely to boost the prime minister's image as Italy, which has had almost 70 governments over the past 80 years, gears up for a national vote in 2027, analysts say. But recent events have complicated her path to re-election.</summary></entry><entry><title>Nigerian police arrest four suspects over alleged organ harvesting</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8f930d2b18f11734a252ac5b9a477d098eec30b36042a95eb0164e43727463ae</id><updated>2026-09-04T12:49:19Z</updated><published>2026-09-04T09:34:36Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260904-nigerian-police-arrest-four-suspects-over-alleged-organ-harvesting--fdece8d4b681.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260904-nigerian-police-arrest-four-suspects-over-alleged-organ-harvesting" /><summary type="html">In Nigeria, the police have arrested four suspects over alleged organ harvesting. Two of the suspects are medical doctors who are accused of carrying out the surgeries to harvest the kidneys. The victims are mainly vulnerable and uneducated youths whose financial desperation is exploited to illegally harvest their kidney for transplant to patients who are often wealthy, as FRANCE 24’s Sam Olukoya reports.</summary></entry><entry><title>Tigray's fragile recovery at risk as drone strikes reignite war fears</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d56c74f8cbc5187d744657b76173f69cc5a44838b9a9210042740329bb800572</id><updated>2026-09-04T12:49:22Z</updated><published>2026-09-04T09:33:01Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260904-tigray-s-fragile-recovery-at-risk-as-drone-strikes-reignite-war-fears--2e64ce60b2a2.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260904-tigray-s-fragile-recovery-at-risk-as-drone-strikes-reignite-war-fears" /><summary type="html">Over the past month, drone strikes have hit several parts of Ethiopia's Tigray region, sparking fears of a renewed war. The last conflict left an estimated 600,000 people dead, making it the deadliest conflict of the 21st century. As the region has not yet rebuilt or recovered from that damage, health experts are warning of the potential impact on patients if another war were to break out. FRANCE 24's Tom Canetty reports.</summary></entry><entry><title>German far right's breakout moment? AfD party eyes outright win in regional election</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:789c0059ce3ede1ea0ee689be7303d873fe517b6e1f0f47e93c5c06d0143f8e3</id><updated>2026-09-04T12:49:26Z</updated><published>2026-09-04T09:29:09Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-debate/20260904-german-far-right-s-breakout-moment-afd-party-eyes-outright-win-in-regional-election--ad40d2f059ef.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-debate/20260904-german-far-right-s-breakout-moment-afd-party-eyes-outright-win-in-regional-election" /><summary type="html">Could Europeans awaken next Monday to another shock bellwether moment? German voters could for the first time since World War II give an outright majority to a far-right party in regional elections. We ask about the AfD's push in Saxony-Anhalt and a charismatic lead candidate whose campaign strives to put charm above the vitriol usually associated with a party with pro-Nazi roots.</summary><category term="The Debate" /></entry><entry><title>Why early warning signs of glacier collapse in Nepal were difficult to detect</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7c07fa69102ae5475544aa8daa7ce2f3518c8f95dff99f24f88d73ba45487734</id><updated>2026-09-04T12:49:29Z</updated><published>2026-09-04T07:24:28Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20260904-nepal-why-early-warning-signs-of-glacier-collapse-were-difficult-to-detect--b6433db61383.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20260904-nepal-why-early-warning-signs-of-glacier-collapse-were-difficult-to-detect" /><summary type="html">The glacier collapse that led to devastating flash floods across the Himalayan region of Nepal and its border with the Chinese autonomous region of Tibet on August 26 was preceded by early warning signs, experts say. But monitoring and emergency alert systems in the region are still insufficient to predict such disasters.</summary><category term="Asia / Pacific" /></entry><entry><title>USS Lincoln crew hits the streets of Thailand's Pattaya after nine-month deployment</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:04ca44e7dd420ffe70f32d4ffa33b0e462d9299a8249d1b39099acafc6f936d8</id><updated>2026-09-04T12:49:32Z</updated><published>2026-09-04T07:02:55Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20260904-uss-lincoln-crew-hits-the-streets-of-thailand-pattaya-after-nine-month-deployment--29255ce7fac8.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20260904-uss-lincoln-crew-hits-the-streets-of-thailand-pattaya-after-nine-month-deployment" /><summary type="html">US sailors and Marines streamed into the Thai resort city of Pattaya Thursday after a record-breaking nine months at sea. Local police said there had so far been no major incidents connected to the 5,000-strong contingent of US service members, though two sailors were sent back to the ship after a drunken bar brawl.</summary><category term="Asia / Pacific" /></entry><entry><title>PSG look for their first Ligue 1 win against Monaco</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d4e94899ea8fb1990da1613d8c667d8dd442da3a7753ce58310c0000af9bce7a</id><updated>2026-09-04T12:49:35Z</updated><published>2026-09-04T06:23:58Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/sports/20260904-psg-look-for-their-first-ligue-1-win-against-monaco--a1f1ed5ff0c1.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/sports/20260904-psg-look-for-their-first-ligue-1-win-against-monaco" /><summary type="html">PSG have still not won a Ligue 1 match this season. After two games, the European champions have recorded two draws. The exact opposite is true of Monaco, who, with two wins from two games, are one of the teams in form at the start of the season. The two Ligue 1 heavyweights will meet on Friday in Paris.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>'Pragmatic international relations': Sánchez seeks to avoid 'further conflict with Rabat'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:22e7ad785ada03eda14ab8e2ea791de072a2a9acb23e52cb01ebf46aed5b83df</id><updated>2026-09-04T12:49:37Z</updated><published>2026-09-04T05:22:52Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260904-pragmatic-international-relations-s_nchez-seeks-to-avoid-further-conflict-with-rabat--c4a5b9cb15c4.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260904-pragmatic-international-relations-s%C3%A1nchez-seeks-to-avoid-further-conflict-with-rabat" /><summary type="html">Delano D'Souza is pleased to welcome Alana Moceri, International Relations Professor at IE School of Politics, Economics and Global Affairs. The migrant crossings at Ceuta have become both a domestic and international political lightning rod. At home, Pedro Sánchez faces opponents who can cast migration in existential terms, with Spain's far right amplifying the rhetoric of "invasion." Internationally, the crisis exposes the geopolitical leverage inherent in control of the border. Ceuta thus emerges as more than a migration crisis: the border becomes at once an instrument of geopolitical leverage, a weapon in Spain's domestic political contest, and a battleground for competing narratives and disinformation.</summary></entry></feed>
